cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use screws in teaching or research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "screws: robotics in Python built on screw theory"
abstract: >-
  Robotics in Python, built on screw theory and written in the notation of Lynch and Park,
  Modern Robotics: rigid-body motions, forward and inverse kinematics, Jacobians,
  manipulability and force ellipsoids, dynamics and trajectories, with the same computations
  as SymPy formulas, pictures of screw axes and Jacobians, and a bridge to the CoppeliaSim
  simulator.
authors:
  - family-names: Picone
    given-names: Rico A. R.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5091-5175"
    affiliation: "Saint Martin's University"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ricopicone/screws"
# the concept DOI: every version of screws, resolving to the latest
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23873253
license: MIT
version: 0.9.1
date-released: 2026-11-01
keywords:
  - robotics
  - screw theory
  - product of exponentials
  - kinematics
  - dynamics
  - education
  - SymPy
  - CoppeliaSim
